<code>assert !Objects.isNull(c) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

Explanation:
- The comment specifies that if the collection `c` is not null, then for every valid index `i` in the list, the element at index `i` in the list should be equal to the element at index `i` in the collection `c`.
- We use `!Objects.isNull(c)` to check if `c` is not null.
- We use `\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size();` to iterate over all valid indices in the list.
- We use `this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i])` to compare the elements at index `i` in the list and the collection.

Note: Since the `get` method is used to retrieve elements from the list and `toArray` method is used to convert the collection to an array, these methods are used to access the elements for comparison.
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i) == c.toArray()[i];</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(c == null) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i) == c.toArray()[i];</code>
